WEBVTT

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.050
I look forward to our meeting today.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.840
Welcome, my tanuki friends.
I'll be observing from here.

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:20.720
We thank you from the bottoms of our hearts

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.110
for taking time out of your busy schedule

00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:26.790
to oversee our tanuki meeting.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.550
Yasaka Heitaro, do as you wish.

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:36.010
By the way, I don't see
Yasaburo-kun anywhere.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:40.200
He's currently on the run since he incurred

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:42.850
the wrath of Benten-sama.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.740
Good grief, he's a rather busy tanuki.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:55.810
Sou-san, please protect our children.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:00.620
<b>Incoming Call
Yashiro</b>

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:00.620
Yes, yes.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.400
What?

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:12.080
"Nasebanaru" to hito wa yuuga

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:12.080
People say, "Where there's 
a will, there's a way"

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.560
Narugamama naseba ii

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.560
But things can just be how they'll be

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:28.210
Nagareru kawa ukabu kobune

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:28.210
A small boat floats along the river

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.110
Doko ni yukuno darouka

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.110
I wonder where it's going

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.320
Ikisaki nado yosou dekinu

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.320
I can't even guess its destination

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.580
Sorega omoshiroki koto

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:41.580
But that's why it's so fun

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:50.710
Kokorozashi wa takaku mokuhyou wa hikuku

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:50.710
My intentions are high, but my goals are low

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:55.770
Aho wo mazerya kekka

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:55.770
When foolishness gets mixed in

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:03.390
Yukai ni nareru

00:01:55.770 --> 00:02:03.390
Everything will be merry

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:09.640
Narugamama ni sawagu mama ni

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:09.640
As things will be, as chaotic as they will be

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.230
Toraburu suramo nenryou sa

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:14.230
Even troubles become fuel

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:18.680
Namikaze tatanai jinsei wa

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:18.680
A life lived without any strife

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:23.200
Chotto bakkari tsumaranai

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:23.200
Can be a bit boring

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.920
Okiraku ni gokuraku ni

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:27.920
Carefree and blissfully

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.500
Kaze ni makasete ikou

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:32.500
Let's let the wind lead us

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.010
Kyou mo bakashite ikou

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:37.010
Let's go trick everyone again today

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.010
<b>Episode Eleven
The Blood of the Tengu, the Blood of the Fool</b>

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.100
Yashiro?!

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.840
I'm fine.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:53.320
You are <i>not</i> fine!

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.290
What in the world happened?

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.900
It's truly awful!

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:01.990
The Trick Denki Bran production machine
that Yashiro was in the middle of creating

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.470
caused an explosion!

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:06.510
That can't be true.

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.450
There's no way it'd explode.

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:10.570
Oh, you're so stubborn!

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:14.750
I'd like to know how you discipline children
in the Shimogamo family.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.240
Yashiro, where were you when it happened?

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:21.750
I was out taking a break.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.260
I'll investigate this myself.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.220
You're not tampering with the evidence!

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.750
Say, Kinkaku.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:33.100
I am truly for all the trouble this caused,

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:36.230
but I think it's a bit early
to jump to conclusions.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.690
Where's Kaisei?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.650
Let me speak with her.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.590
Kaisei's shut herself into her room.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.690
She's been rather mopey of late.

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:48.120
She's just at that difficult age.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.740
She's shut in her room even
after something like this?

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:55.420
Are you plotting something again?

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.170
Nii-san! I found something strange.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.760
Oh, my! This is...

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.720
What's this doing in your laboratory?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:05.740
I don't know!

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:07.720
I've never even seen it before!

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:11.880
This is the German gun that
the Nidaime was looking for, isn't it?

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:13.760
What?

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.800
What's the meaning of this?

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:28.950
Wow, proper rails sure are wide.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:31.530
You're running just fine.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:37.460
Once this is all settled, I think
I'm going to go back to Shikoku.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:39.840
Sounds good.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.060
I'm sure that Kincho girl
will be happy about that.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:46.990
Come back again.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:50.890
Take me to Cape Muroto
in the Trick Eizan train next time.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:57.350
Come to think of it, what was her name?

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.780
What? You don't even know?

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:01.610
Come on, man.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:03.820
Her name is Seiran.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.020
It means "a wave of stars."

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:09.500
That's a very cosmic and lovely name.

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:12.210
It's kind of like Kaisei's.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.470
Well, of course it is.

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:20.840
Seiran was named by none other than
the Trick Magister, Shimogamo Souichiro.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:21.930
Huh?!

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.760
They got us.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:37.100
We're headed straight
for the Friday Club's hot pot.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.640
Tenmaya has arrived.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.610
Good work.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:50.460
I've come to deliver the tanuki.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.990
Well done, Tenmaya.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.930
Now we can enjoy our hot pot.

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.080
So, has Yasaburo-kun been excommunicated?

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.590
It seems Benten-san was wrong about him.

00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:07.940
He was a pretty amusing young man.

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:10.090
It's nothing for you to worry about.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:14.220
By the way, where did you
acquire these tanuki?

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.980
In that one artist's yard.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:23.730
Our dear friend, Ebisugawa Kureichiro-san,
was kind enough to suggest the place.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:28.860
I headed right over and was lucky enough
to find these two in the middle of a tryst.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:32.990
Sadly, they will have to
finish it in a hot pot.

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:37.330
By the way, Tenmaya,
you seem a bit wealthier.

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:43.230
Ebisugawa Kureichiro-san
wanted my gun quite badly,

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:47.340
so I sold it to him at a fair price.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.790
But you have your gun right there.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.660
Oh, would you look at that.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:55.720
How bizarre...

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:58.310
You tricked Ebisugawa, didn't you?

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:00.850
I just sold him some dreams.

00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.980
Tenmaya, you truly are a villain.

00:07:04.730 --> 00:07:07.370
You will eventually fall straight to Hell.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:11.020
I feel the breeze from hell once again today.

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:15.780
Please don't say something so scary.

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:20.500
They might be coming for you soon.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:30.950
Oh, Tenmaya-san. I thought that
I smelled something strange,

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.680
but I guess it was just you.

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.070
That's a rather harsh thing to say.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:38.680
This is all because Yasaburo-kun ran off.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:41.500
Which basically means I was
wiping your behind, Benten-san.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:44.290
I'd rather be engulfed in the flames of hell

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:47.230
than let you touch me in any way.

00:07:48.850 --> 00:07:53.380
I'm working myself to the bone
for you, but not a word of thanks.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.120
You excite me so much.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:58.040
Unattainable flowers
never bow down to others.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:08.090
Oh? Apparently, even demons
can cry sometimes.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:15.110
It's a pity that I'll have to eat you.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:19.600
Even so, I'm going to eat you.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:28.030
I think it's about time.

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.190
The Trick Magister has been chosen!

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:32.400
Hold it right there!

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.470
What is the meaning of this, Kinkaku?

00:08:34.470 --> 00:08:36.400
Quiet down.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:37.250
The Nidaime...

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.620
You can scold me all you want later.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.050
This is the German air gun

00:08:43.050 --> 00:08:47.880
that shot our father, Ebisugawa Soun, dead.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:56.370
Shimogamo Yashiro caused an explosion
at the factory a little while ago.

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:57.470
Yashiro did?!

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.510
We happened to find this
while we were investigating.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.390
I was completely astonished.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:06.570
Why would Yashiro be hiding such a thing

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.770
in his own laboratory?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.190
It couldn't be.

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:17.010
I'm sure Yashiro-kun will
eventually admit to everything,

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:18.910
but we'd rather not let him escape,

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:23.580
so we're keeping him
at the factory with your mother.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.620
How dare you...

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.380
Wait...

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.140
It's a set up.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.590
The Ebisugawas are setting us up!

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:34.860
We have solid proof right here.

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.900
Why did you hide it?

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:42.090
Because you used this gun to kill our father.

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:43.390
You tanuki killer!

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.610
I'm so smart that I figured it all out.

00:09:46.610 --> 00:09:48.980
I've seen through all your plans.

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:54.230
You had Yasaburo do the assassination
and Yashiro hide the evidence.

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:58.560
Meanwhile, you'd feign ignorance
and become the Trick Magister.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.000
Such furry and deep team work!

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.990
Your brotherly love is almost pathetic.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:07.540
I still can't believe it.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.750
Assassinating my father?

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:18.300
Don't you dare try to feign ignorance
and become the Trick Magister.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.390
Shimogamo Yasaburo has been
captured by the Friday Club.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:26.970
Yasaburo?!

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:36.360
Well, I mean, it <i>is</i> Yasaburo.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:40.140
Yasaburo incurred the wrath of Benten-sama

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:44.160
because he went out on a limb
for tanuki society!

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:49.460
How can all of you just stand around
after hearing that he's been caught?!

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:02.530
So it was you.

00:11:06.690 --> 00:11:08.340
To hell with tradition!

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:10.340
To hell with the future of the tanuki world!

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:11.560
To hell with the Trick Magister!

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.570
Now you've said it, Yaichiro.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:17.570
I am Yaichiro, the eldest son
of Shimogamo Souichiro!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:22.510
I am the pathetic son who didn't inherit
all of the magnificent blood of his father!

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:26.200
But I have the blood of the fool
running through my veins.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.990
Even if I sink to the bottom
of a steel pot myself,

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:31.420
I will save my brother.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:34.830
You all can fool around here all you want.

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:40.680
If you want to be the Trick Magister
so badly, you can have the stupid title!

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:44.930
Gyokuran?

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:48.060
I'm sorry, Gyokuran.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.380
In the end, I'm nothing more than a fool.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.660
I knew that.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:54.610
That's why I'm here.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.990
<b>Nishizaki Genemon Shoten</b>

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.990
<b>Sukiyaki Restaurant</b>

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.990
<b>Akegarasu</b>

00:12:06.890 --> 00:12:09.320
My butt's getting really cold.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:15.020
This will be a year-end banquet we won't
forget thanks to those Ebisugawa dummies.

00:12:17.180 --> 00:12:19.750
Hello. I've brought your dinner.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:24.110
Say, Ginkaku.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:29.680
You don't actually believe that we shot
and killed Ebisugawa-san, do you?

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.650
I can't really say anything.

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:36.350
Please, Ginkaku.

00:12:36.350 --> 00:12:38.400
Let us out of here.

00:12:40.060 --> 00:12:42.640
I can't let you out of your cage,

00:12:43.590 --> 00:12:46.960
but it might be a good idea
to discuss this with Kaisei.

00:12:51.530 --> 00:12:55.420
Does this mean that Yaichiro-niisan
can't become the Trick Magister?

00:12:55.690 --> 00:12:59.060
This has all become rather complicated.

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:02.740
I'm sure Yasaburo-niichan
will do something about it.

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:04.130
I'm not sure he can.

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.370
He doesn't know anything about it.

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:08.860
What should I do?

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:10.680
Kaisei's not in her room.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:12.560
What do you mean?

00:13:12.560 --> 00:13:14.730
I found this letter.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:18.480
<b>I'm eloping with Yasaburo</b>

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:17.230
Oh, my...

00:13:26.960 --> 00:13:28.550
Akegarasu?

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:42.250
Father, have I already ended up in a hot pot?

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.590
No, you haven't. You're just sleeping.

00:13:46.110 --> 00:13:48.480
This is a dream.

00:13:49.420 --> 00:13:53.380
Why are you in your tanuki form, Father?

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:56.870
I'm not exactly able to transform anymore.

00:13:57.250 --> 00:14:00.650
But you should, since you're in my dream.

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.960
You can't just do anything you want.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.360
It is a dream, after all.

00:14:09.270 --> 00:14:11.670
Father, you're an awful tanuki.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:16.340
You went off on your own, picked fights
with tengu, made an enemy of Soun,

00:14:16.780 --> 00:14:21.900
and then left your family behind
and ended up in a tanuki hot pot.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:27.480
You may have been prepared,
but we were all in shock.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.340
I'm truly sorry.

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:33.430
It was all because of my fool's blood.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:38.770
We have a tendency of blaming
everything on our fool's blood.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:42.500
So you can't really say anything
about your father, can you?

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:44.120
You're right.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:47.560
The son of a frog is a frog;
the son of a furball is a furball.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:53.700
Yasaburo, are you enjoying your life?

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:56.830
I am enjoying my life.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:01.580
So much that I'm about to
end up at the bottom of a pot.

00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:05.670
When that time comes, I will come for you.

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:07.950
Thank you, Father.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.890
But I can't fall into the pot just yet.

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:14.770
I was thinking that if it came down to it,

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:17.730
I'd just smile and end up
in the pot like you did,

00:15:18.230 --> 00:15:21.260
but I can't drag Kaisei down with me,

00:15:21.260 --> 00:15:24.040
and I have plenty left to do in this world.

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:26.400
And that's fine.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.900
Eventually, everyone follows this path.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.690
There's no point in rushing.

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:35.040
How can you smile when your own son

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:37.830
is about to fall into a hot pot, Father?

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:39.820
We are tanuki.

00:15:40.220 --> 00:15:42.870
There is no time when
we shouldn't be smiling.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.090
Take care of Akadama-sensei for me.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:54.870
You still have plenty left to do.

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:12.950
Pompoko Mask has come to save you.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:18.600
I hear we got two of them tonight.

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.640
Well, well! Tenmaya-san's outdone himself.

00:16:21.640 --> 00:16:24.920
I can't eat two tanuki.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:29.380
Who are you?

00:16:29.560 --> 00:16:32.720
The protector of tanuki, Pompoko Mask!

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:37.110
All right, Yodogawa-san, we get it.

00:16:37.110 --> 00:16:40.180
Honestly, you're so hopeless. Let's get him.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:46.560
Those spikes are poisonous!

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:56.710
We're flying?

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:04.180
We don't want to hurt you,
so just stay still!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.880
We'll let you go.
Just leave the tanuki behind!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.880
<b>Men</b>

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:17.720
Let us go!

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:19.090
Professor...

00:17:19.090 --> 00:17:20.440
Leave them behind!

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:24.310
Oh, my. What's going on out here?

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:31.700
Yodogawa-sensei, you can't
keep the tanuki all to yourself.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:45.870
Why are there tigers again this year?!

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:49.130
Well, this is all rather troublesome.

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.970
My trip to Hawaii...

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:55.920
I have a proposal for you, sir.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:58.090
What is it, Kinkaku?

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.570
Make it.

00:17:59.570 --> 00:18:03.310
Why not make Kureichiro-niisan
the acting Trick Magister?

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:08.560
Then you can fly off to your island
without worry, Yasaka-san.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:11.940
The elders will eventually decide

00:18:11.940 --> 00:18:14.990
who will officially be the Trick Magister.

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:19.200
That's an unusually bright idea
coming from you.

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:22.470
I don't think there's
an issue making Kureichiro

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:25.600
the acting Trick Magister for the time being.

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.490
I, Ebisugawa Kureichiro,

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:37.540
would be honored to take
the title of Trick Magister.

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:40.300
I still have much to learn,

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:45.310
but I will work myself to the bone
for the tanuki world.

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:47.210
Good grief.

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:48.270
Are you quite done?

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:53.510
Could I have my gun back now?

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:56.250
Oh, yes, yes, yes, yes...

00:18:56.250 --> 00:18:57.160
Here you go!

00:19:00.260 --> 00:19:01.670
This is a fake.

00:19:01.670 --> 00:19:02.430
Huh?

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:05.820
You couldn't even kill a goldfish
with this toy,

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.540
seeing as it can't shoot anything.

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:11.040
What is the meaning of this?

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:13.040
This can't be.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:17.800
This is a strange turn
of events, Kureichiro-kun.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:20.630
I do beg your pardon, Nidaime,

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.890
but that can't be true.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:24.510
But you see...

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:27.250
I'm telling you that it is a fake.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.320
But that's impossible.

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:35.440
Oh, well, if it isn't Yajiro.

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:37.620
I heard you left on a trip.

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:42.780
I had something to tell you all,
so I returned post haste from Shikoku.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.540
Ah, so this must be Kureichiro.

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:56.540
Yeah, he's definitely Kureichiro.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:20:00.660
So I have to wonder,
who does that make me?

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:01.760
How would we know?!

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:03.760
Who are you anyway?

00:20:04.240 --> 00:20:06.760
I'm Ebisugawa Kureichiro.

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:08.490
Stop lying!

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:11.100
Ebisugawa Kureichiro is
sitting right over there!

00:20:11.550 --> 00:20:14.050
Did all your eyes and noses stop working?

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:16.310
The man sitting over there

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:18.860
is Ebisugawa Soun.

00:20:30.760 --> 00:20:33.120
Yaichiro, look out for the gun!

00:20:57.670 --> 00:20:59.190
Why, you...

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:04.020
Kaisei-chan isn't waking up.

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:06.000
She was shot and sedated.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:07.820
What an awful thing to do!

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.780
What in the world is going on?

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:12.120
We can't escape like this.

00:21:22.670 --> 00:21:24.720
What's the meaning of all this?!

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.380
There!

00:21:28.120 --> 00:21:31.130
<i>Our father, Shimogamo Souichiro,</i>

00:21:31.580 --> 00:21:35.640
<i>was such a fool that he danced
on the edge of a hot pot,</i>

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:40.200
<i>and because he did,
he left many legends behind.</i>

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:44.070
The skies of Kyoto belong to me!

00:21:44.070 --> 00:21:46.780
The skies of Kyoto belong to the tengu!

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:49.370
Who do you think you are, you human!

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:55.730
<i>"It's because of the fool's blood,"
my father said.</i>

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:09.350
Tsuki wo medetewa toki ni wa nusunde

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:09.350
While gazing lovingly at the 
moon, at times, she steals it

00:22:09.350 --> 00:22:14.140
Kimagure na kanojo wa ah

00:22:09.350 --> 00:22:14.140
Whimsical as she may be, ah

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:18.630
Kawabe de hitori hoho ni namida

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:18.630
As she stands by the riverside 
alone, secretly her tears

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:22.950
Utsukushiku tayutau

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:22.950
Quiver beautifully upon her cheeks

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:34.740
Boku no te tori nagara 
kokoro wa dokoka ni ukabu

00:22:22.950 --> 00:22:34.740
She takes my hand, as her 
heart floats away somewhere

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:39.260
Kasaneta te ni wa mada nukumori

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:39.260
I still feel that warmth from her held hand

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:43.630
Setsunai yume no sono ato saki

00:22:39.260 --> 00:22:43.630
Somewhere beyond this sentimental dream

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.250
Demo kimi no me wa harukana 
mirai wo miteitane

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.250
But you were already looking 
far into the future

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:57.890
Zutto zutto oikaketayo

00:22:53.250 --> 00:22:57.890
I always chased after you

00:22:57.890 --> 00:23:02.270
Kimi ga kizutsuku toki mo

00:22:57.890 --> 00:23:02.270
Even when you were hurt

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:11.600
Sotto mabuta ni yakitsuita kimi no sugata ni

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:11.600
The vision of you that's 
softly imprinted on my eyes

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:16.540
Ima mata tooku e to ah

00:23:11.600 --> 00:23:16.540
Once again, you fly far away, ah

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:28.860
Tondeiku kimi wa hora Kanata no hito

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:28.860
You are a person far beyond

00:23:30.580 --> 00:23:32.590
Disputes between tanuki
and disputes between tengu.

00:23:32.590 --> 00:23:34.100
To eat or be eaten.

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.810
Which awaits for me tomorrow?

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:37.770
All I can say with certainty is...

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Episode Twelve
The Red String of Fate</b>

00:23:37.770 --> 00:23:40.180
A fun thing is a good thing.
